  "worked_solution": "To find the coterminal angles of a given angle $\\theta $, we add and subtract integer multiples of ${360}^{\u2218}:$\n\nLet's start by adding multiples of ${360}^{\u2218}$ to $-{95}^{\u2218}$:\n\n- $-{95}^{\u2218}+{360}^{\u2218}={265}^{\u2218}$\n\n- $-{95}^{\u2218}+2\\cdot {360}^{\u2218}={625}^{\u2218}\\,\u2713$\n\nOf the given values, there is no angle greater than ${625}^{\u2218}.$ So we can stop there.\n\nNow, let's subtract multiples of ${360}^{\u2218}$ from $-{95}^{\u2218}$\n\n- $-{95}^{\u2218}-{360}^{\u2218}=-{455}^{\u2218}\\,\u2713$\n\nOf the given angles, only ${625}^{\u2218}$ and $-{455}^{\u2218}$ are coterminal with $-{95}^{\u2218}.$\n\nSo the correct answer is I and III only.",
